  "description": "SUPPIF crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C66 H57 Ce2 Mn3 O26,2.35(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 8 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.712-3.743 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.49-130.79°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ce2Mn3O5(O2CPh)9(MeOH)3].",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
